2026-01-01 no assignment: the elided amount is known for the assertion below it
  a  5 EUR
  b
  b  0 EUR = -5 EUR

2026-01-02 an assignment in the transaction: c's amount is added at the end of it
  c
  d  = 5 EUR
  c  0 EUR = 0 EUR

2026-01-03 so the next day it is there
  c  0 EUR = -5 EUR
  y

2026-01-04 an assignment of m itself sees a balance without the elided amount; it is added after
  m
  f  = 5 EUR
  m  = -7 EUR

2026-01-05 -7 plus the elided 2
  m  0 EUR = -5 EUR
  y

2026-01-06 a virtual assignment counts as an assignment, and so does a zero difference
  g  5 EUR
  h
  (v)  = 0 EUR
  h  0 EUR = 0 EUR

2026-01-07 plain transactions: posting dates split the transaction
  k  5 EUR
  k  1 EUR  ; date:2026-03-01
  z

2026-01-08 asserting before the 1st of March
  k  0 EUR = 5 EUR
  y

2026-01-09 an assignment in the transaction: it is processed as a whole, at its date
  l  = 5 EUR
  l  1 EUR  ; date:2026-03-01
  z

2026-01-10 so the dated posting is already there
  l  0 EUR = 6 EUR
  y
